---
import { getLangFromUrl, useMetaTranslations } from '../../i18n/utils';

import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const lang = getLangFromUrl(Astro.url);
const tm = useMetaTranslations(lang);

---

<Layout 
  title="About Us | fxlotsizecalculator.com"
  description="Learn more about fxlotsizecalculator.com and our mission to provide traders with the best risk management tools."
>
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-24">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-ink mb-8">About Us</h1>
    
    <div class="prose prose-slate dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6 text-body">
      <p class="text-lg">
        Welcome to <strong>fxlotsizecalculator.com</strong>.
      </p>

      <p>
        Our mission is simple: to provide traders of all experience levels with a blazing fast, completely free, and highly accurate tool to manage their risk across all asset classes.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink mt-8">Why We Built This</h2>
      <p>
        Risk management is the absolute foundation of profitable trading. However, calculating position sizes manually, especially across different asset classes like Forex, Gold, Indices, and Crypto, can be tedious and prone to human error. A single misplaced decimal point can blow an account.
      </p>
      <p>
        We built this tool so traders can focus on the charts, not the math. By saving your preferences locally and offering instantaneous calculations, we aim to be the last lot size calculator you'll ever need.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink mt-8">Our Philosophy</h2>
      <p>
        We believe that professional-grade trading tools should be accessible to everyone. That is why fxlotsizecalculator.com is free, respects your privacy by doing the math locally in your browser, and requires no account registrations.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
